# Prefetch on press

A press on a way to home, a stream's page or a group asks the api for that page's first data on `pointerdown`, ~100-200ms before the click and the route land (docs/spec.md "Prefetch on press"). **One** path does it: `frontend/src/infra/prefetch.ts`.

- **A link** (`<Link to=…>`, any `<a href>` to one of those paths) needs nothing: the one capturing listener on the document (`installPrefetch`, main.tsx) sees it. A link whose click does something else instead (opens a popup, reloads the document) says `data-prefetch="off"`, as `ProfileLink` does while the popup is on.
- **Anything else that navigates there by hand** (`navigate('/')`, `navigate(profilePath(name))`, a card or button with an `onClick`) spreads `usePrefetchOnPointerDown(path)` on the element; pass `null` while the click would not navigate.
- **No other prefetching.** No `onMouseEnter` fetches, no `queryClient.prefetchQuery`, no second cache, no hand-rolled `pointerdown` handler calling `api.*`.
- **A page's loader** owns what is asked, beside itself: `onPrefetch(kind, fn)` in its atom module calls `prefetch(key, topic, 'drop' | 'hold', ask)` with the same request the loader makes, and the loader asks `takePrefetched(key)?.answer ?? api.…()` after it has watched its topic. A new first request on one of those pages goes in both places with the same key.
- **Reads, and the watch page's warm peer.** A press that goes nowhere costs GETs (and the grant, a read despite its `POST`) that expire in 5s. The one thing beyond reads: `/watch/<name>` also makes its peer with the offer set and opens the video socket (`warmOnPress` in watch-atoms.ts), sending nothing on it, one at a time, closed after 5s unless the page takes it. Never a write on a press, never a setup frame or a chat socket, and no peer or socket for any other page.
- **A new route** joins by adding its kind to `prefetchRouteOf` and an `onPrefetch` beside its loader. A route whose page is a lazy chunk (`router.tsx`) has its chunk loaded by `prefetchRoute` too, through the same loader the router uses (`loadServerPage` for a group).
- **A stream's page loaded straight** has no press: index.html's boot script asks for the grant and warms the peer and socket instead, and `start` takes them (`takeBoot`). A new first request on that page goes there too.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — a press-time fetch of its own, and a button that waits for the click
<div onMouseDown={() => void api.watch(name)} onClick={() => navigate(`/watch/${name}`)} />

// ✅ GOOD — a link: nothing to add
<Link to={`/watch/${encodeURIComponent(name)}`}>{name}</Link>

// ✅ GOOD — a button that navigates
const press = usePrefetchOnPointerDown('/');
<IconButton label="picture in picture" {...press} onClick={toCorner} />
```
